The legal texts come from the Cámara de Diputados del H. Congreso de la Unión:

  Fuente: Cámara de Diputados del H. Congreso de la Unión, Secretaría General, Secretaría de Servicios
  Parlamentarios, Leyes Federales Vigentes (www.diputados.gob.mx/LeyesBiblio), as archived by the Internet Archive
  (web.archive.org), copies captured 2006-2026, retrieved 28 October 2026.

They are official legislative texts of the United Mexican States. The Ley Federal del Derecho de Autor, art. 14,
fracción VIII, excludes legislative, regulatory, administrative and judicial texts from copyright protection. The
Cámara de Diputados publishes no separate licence for LeyesBiblio; the texts are reproduced with the attribution
above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each archived copy of the consolidated text was converted to one Markdown file per
provision, one paragraph per line; spacing, quotes, dashes and runs of dots were normalised; the Cámara's paragraph
notes ("Párrafo reformado DOF ...") were removed from the text and used only to credit the amending decree; and the
copies were arranged as git commits credited to the decrees that made each change, on the day each took effect. The
wording of the law was not changed. The Cámara de Diputados does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
